'''Subway Boss Emmet''' (Japanese: '''サブウェイマスタークダリ''' ''Subway Master Kudari'') is one of the leaders of the [[Battle Subway]] in {{game3|Black and White|Pokémon Black, White|s}}, {{B2W2|Black 2, and White 2}}, along with his brother, [[Ingo]].

==In the core series games==
Emmet can be battled in a [[Double Battle]] on the [[Battle Subway]]'s Double Train once the player has acquired a 20 win streak, and on the Super Double Train once the player has acquired a 48 win streak. He can also be fought alongside his brother [[Ingo]] in a [[Multi Battle]] on the Multi Train once the player has acquired a 20 win streak, and on the Super Multi Train once the player has acquired a 48 win streak. His teams in both {{2v2|Black|White}} and {{2v2|Black|White|2}} are identical. In Black 2 and White 2 only, the brothers can also be faced in a one-time Multi Battle in front of the Gear Station.

While Emmet does not physically appear in {{g|Legends: Arceus}}, he is indirectly referred to by Ingo, who had wound up in the ancient [[Hisui]] sometime before and lost most of his memories. In {{g|Legends: Z-A}}, an exhibit at the [[Lumiose Museum]] mentions Ingo having disappeared from Hisui one day, while an NPC in [[Bleu Sector 8]] mentions wanting to challenge Ingo and Emmet aboard the Multi Train, indicating that Emmet has reunited with his brother in the present day and is running the Battle Subway with him as usual once more.

